; ted-readline-token-before-eof (#379): a byte >= $80 as the last byte of
; a file was stored as the first byte of a token pair, the 0 behind it as
; its second: detok read on behind the end of the line.  A tokenised file
; (lines end in 0 bytes): lines "x" and "a" + $E4 (the start of a token
; pair, cut by the end of the file), loaded under blitz2, SAVE.  Correct
; (the fix: the half token is dropped): line 2 is saved as "a"; the
; original saves the half token (a, $E4, 0).  (It also shows unknown
; tokens read from behind the line, "a?????..." - memory contents, not
; compared.)  A tokenised file, so that the byte is a token start
; whatever readline does with a byte >= $80 of a text file (#374).
; @fixed #379
; @file bo.bas "x\x00a\xe4"
; @source F bo.bas
; @expect data bo.bas "x\x00a\x00"
timeout 10
wait req "OKEE DOKEE"
gad 1
wait screen
menu 0 2
wait freq "Name to save file as"
freq ok
wait screen
menu 0 9
wait exit
